From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:44:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] manager: make the identified push service public

Manager::identified_push_service() returns the cached credentialed
PushService, but it is private, so a client cannot make an
authenticated request the manager has no wrapper for. purple-presage
needs one for 1:1 calls: GET /v2/calling/relays returns the TURN/STUN
servers and their credentials, which are only issued to the account.

Make the existing accessor public rather than add a calling-specific
one.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 presage/src/manager/registered.rs | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/presage/src/manager/registered.rs b/presage/src/manager/registered.rs
index 8445433f1..f20596eef 100644
--- a/presage/src/manager/registered.rs
+++ b/presage/src/manager/registered.rs
@@ -204,8 +204,9 @@ impl<S: Store> Manager<S, Registered> {
 
     /// Returns a clone of a cached push service (with credentials).
     ///
-    /// If no service is yet cached, it will create and cache one.
-    fn identified_push_service(&self) -> PushService {
+    /// If no service is yet cached, it will create and cache one. Clients can use it for
+    /// authenticated requests the manager does not wrap, such as `GET /v2/calling/relays`.
+    pub fn identified_push_service(&self) -> PushService {
         self.state.identified_push_service()
     }
 
-- 
